      "role": "user",
      "content": "those sound good, but some people would argue that things like \"collective ownership\" and \"universal services\" basically destroy individual incentive and personal freedom. like, if nobody can really own anything or get ahead, why would anyone work hard? how would the manifesto address those criticisms without just sounding like it's ignoring them?",
